{% extends 'base.html.twig' %}

{% block title %}About Bloggy{% endblock %}

{% block body %}
<div class="container my-5">
    <h1 class="mb-4">About Bloggy</h1>

    <p class="lead">
        <strong>Bloggy</strong> is a modern and intuitive blogging platform,
        designed to share your ideas, experiences, and stories with an active community.
        Whether you're a reader or an author, Bloggy makes publishing and reading articles
        simple and enjoyable.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-5">Our Mission</h2>
    <p>
        Bloggy aims to provide a safe and friendly space where everyone can express
        their creativity, discover new content, and interact with other enthusiasts.
        We focus on content quality and mutual respect among users.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-5">Technologies Used</h2>
    <p>
        Bloggy was developed with modern technologies to ensure performance
        and reliability:
    </p>
    <ul>
        <li>Symfony: a robust and flexible PHP framework</li>
        <li>Twig: a templating engine for clear and maintainable views</li>
        <li>HTML, CSS, and Bootstrap: a responsive and modern interface</li>
        <li>MySQL: efficient management of user and article data</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="mt-5">User Policy</h2>
    <p>
        To ensure a pleasant experience for everyone, we ask our users to adhere to the following rules:
    </p>
    <ul>
        <li>Maintain respectful behavior towards all members.</li>
        <li>Do not publish offensive, discriminatory, or illegal content.</li>
        <li>Protect personal information and respect others' privacy.</li>
        <li>Take responsibility for the content you publish.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="mt-5">Contact</h2>
    <p>
        For any questions, suggestions, or technical support, feel free to contact us:
        <a href="mailto:support@bloggy.com">support@bloggy.com</a>
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-5">About the Developer</h2>
    <p>
        Bloggy was developed within an academic framework to practice modern web development
        with Symfony, Twig, and MVC architecture. The goal was to create a functional,
        secure, and user-friendly platform for everyone.
    </p>

    <p class="mt-4">
        Thank you for visiting <strong>Bloggy</strong> and contributing to our community.
    </p>
</div>
{% endblock %}